The issue occurred due to grails version upgrade. The dispCount was coming null due to which it did not enter inside notification method.

Hibernate uses a first-level cache (session-level cache) to manage entities.

When we updated dispCount directly using SQL, Hibernate's cache was not aware of this update.

When we later retrieved the object using Hibernate (get() or findById()), it fetched the entity from the cache instead of querying the database, causing dispCount to remain null.


